From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 02:19:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: implement RGB32 uniform texel buffers

Metal has no three-component 32-bit texture-buffer format, so a view of one
is read through the GPU address the descriptor carries, with the bounds test
the shader would otherwise get from Metal.

That second path must not reach a shader that never uses it. A descriptor
still names a Metal texture in every case -- a view Metal cannot express
carries a texture in the single-component sibling format over its own memory
-- so the native fetch is issued unconditionally and only the raw read sits
behind the format test. Splitting the common fetch across a format branch
instead costs its loads and its read the memory-level parallelism a loop of
fetches depends on: it doubles the GPU time of a descriptor-indexing loop on
a device where no descriptor is ever raw.

The sibling texture's own texels are never the answer, so it need only be a
valid texture rather than cover every component, and a raw descriptor's
offset word carries the format flag, which puts the unconditional read's
coordinate far outside it. Metal's own robustness returns zero there and the
format test discards it.
---
